hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"227","On the authority of Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, they were sitting, and the Ansar who were present said: Not until it flows. Abu Musa said: I will bring you the news. So he went to Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her, and greeted her. Then he said: I want to ask you about something that I am ashamed of. She said: Do not be ashamed. To ask about something that you would ask your mother who gave birth to you about, for I am only your mother. He said: I said: What necessitates washing? She said: I fell upon the expert. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he sits among its four people, and the circumcision touches the circumcision, it is obligatory ""washing"""
